# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PRIVACY — NEVER COMMIT THESE
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The private re-identification mapping links pseudonymous student labels back
# to real identities. Committing it would breach the ethics approval under which
# this study was conducted (IUG Ethical Research Committee, No. 2026/29), which
# was granted on the basis that all released data are de-identified.
#
# Note: git history is permanent. A file committed and later deleted REMAINS
# recoverable from the history and must be purged with git-filter-repo or the
# repository recreated.
PRIVATE_ID_Mapping_DO_NOT_PUBLISH.xlsx
*ID_Mapping*
*id_mapping*
*Mapping*
*mapping*
*DO_NOT_PUBLISH*
*deident*
*reident*
*re-ident*
*PRIVATE*
*private*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# RAW DATASET
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The seven anonymized examination files are archived on Zenodo with a DOI
# (10.5281/zenodo.20366538) and are not duplicated here. Zenodo is the citable,
# archival home; GitHub is not. Keeping one canonical copy prevents the two from
# drifting apart.
#
# The derived file results/instance_level_features.csv IS committed, so scripts
# 02, 04 and 05 reproduce every reported analysis without the raw files. Only
# script 01 (feature engineering) needs them.
data/*.xlsx
data/*.xls
data/*.csv
!data/README.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.Python
env/
venv/
.venv/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
.ipynb_checkpoints/
.pytest_cache/

